## Scope

Follow [zotero/zotero#6054](https://github.com/zotero/zotero/pull/6054)
after submission by ticket 0727. Read the PR page for maintainer response and
CI, make requested changes on the fork branch, and record the upstream outcome.
`SYNC.md` owns the live status; this ticket owns the work and its evidence.

## Remaining verification from 0727

- Run Remove → install replacement through a real Zotero Add-ons window, with
  the pending removal present, and observe whether the new add-on survives.
- Run the control: a genuinely pending removal still completes when the window
  closes. The submitted module test passed; the real UI path has not run.
- Record any version uplift or changed Firefox `addon-list.mjs` patch anchors.

## Review findings already on the PR page

Every review on zotero/zotero#6054 was posted by the author's own GitHub
account — internal reviews and Claude Opus reviews — and each is recorded as
COMMENTED, not as an upstream verdict. No maintainer response, formal approval,
CI check or merge is recorded on the page. `SYNC.md` says the same.

The second review (submitted at `2fe028c`) reads "## Verdict: APPROVED", with
five findings it marked "(none blocking)", headings and key sentences verbatim:

1. "`return` inside the teardown loop abandons the rest of the snapshot." On
   reconnect mid-loop the remaining entries are "neither finalized nor still in
   the set"; `continue` "would not depend on it."
2. "The correctness of the guard rests on `AddonWrapper` identity, and its
   failure mode is silent." "no test here can catch it, since the tests hand
   back the same object by construction."
3. "`disconnectedCallback` is now async and nothing awaits it, so a rejection is
   unhandled."
4. "Test coverage: the suite is real but unreachable." "`app/scripts/tests/` is
   new and holds only this file; there is no npm script, no CI step, and the
   test needs an argument pointing at a file extracted from a built `omni.ja`.
   It will not run unless someone remembers to run it, so it cannot protect the
   next uplift — the `replace_line` abort is doing that work." Two gaps named
   inside the suite: no case with more than one add-on in the snapshot, and no
   case where `getAddonByID` resolves to `null`/`undefined` or rejects.
5. "Minor, build-script robustness." `remove_line` and `replace_line` act on
   every matching line, so a future second occurrence "changes more than
   intended and stays silent about it."

Later reviews on the same page, same account, move past it: one at `c1bf7a4`
(BLOCKED, on a stale pending-uninstall wrapper restored after a replacement) and
a re-review at `66c1f8a` (APPROVED). The findings above are carried so they
survive the PR page, not as the page's current disposition.

## Exit criteria

The PR has an upstream disposition, requested revisions are resolved, and the
real UI arm and control have results or specific not-run reasons. If merged,
confirm the behavior in an upstream build before closing. Local sitter guards
are tracked separately in 0814.
